o &quot;The Pile&quot; as a lowly social worker. There he counsels gangbanging foster-kid robots and confiscates chimera-children from deadbeat half-wolf parents. Till one day a case goes horribly sideways and Karl is drawn into a sordid conspiracy that could threaten the strained fabric of Human-Robot-Hybrid civilization -- or save it.<br><br><strong>FEATURES</strong><br>-15+ hours of gameplay.<br>-An original dystopic sci-fi world and story that will (hopefully) make you question some of your core beliefs. Or at least my sanity<br>-Tricky yet satisfying, point-n-click detective work, interspersed with tense action shootouts.<br>-Handpainted, uber-gritty, noir futureland. Makes Mad Max and Rick Deckard crap their pants.<br>-Endless bombardment of witty one-liners from hardboiled cyberpunk.<br><br><strong>PRICE</strong> - $14.99<br><br><i>(Content Warning: This game contains imagery relating to violent abductions that may be shocking to some players.)</i><br><br><i>(Warning: Game contains imagery that may affect players with photosensitive epilepsy.)</i>",
